least squares line ŷ = a + bx): b = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) ÷ Σ(x − x̄)²; a = ȳ − b × x̄; r = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) ÷ √(Σ(x − x̄)² × Σ(y − ȳ)²).<br>2. ŷ = 2,2 + 0,6 × 4,5 = 2,2 + 2,7<br>3. = 4,9"},{"text":"Find r.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"r","a":"0.77","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Find Σ(y − ȳ)² first.","steps":"1. Formulas (least squares line ŷ = a + bx): b = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) ÷ Σ(x − x̄)²; a = ȳ − b × x̄; r = Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) ÷ √(Σ(x − x̄)² × Σ(y − ȳ)²).<br>2. Σ(y − ȳ)² = 4 + 0 + 1 + 0 + 1 = 6<br>3. r = 6 ÷ √(10 × 6) = 6 ÷ √60 = 0,77"}]}